      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Defect:** Casting the 32-bit cycle count to `uint64_t` *before* subtraction breaks wrap-around arithmetic.\n\nIf `sys_clock_cycle_get_32()` wraps around during the `crec_usleep()` call (e.g., `start_time \u003d 0xFFFFFFF0` and `now \u003d 0x00000010`), `now` will be numerically smaller than `start_time`. Because both are cast to `uint64_t` before the subtraction, `now - start_time` will yield a massive 64-bit value instead of the correct small time difference.\n\nStore the 32-bit cycle counts in `uint32_t` variables, subtract them first, and *then* cast the result to `uint64_t`.\n\n```c\n#if defined(CONFIG_TIMER_HAS_64BIT_CYCLE_COUNTER)\n\tuint64_t start_time \u003d sys_clock_cycle_get_64();\n#else\n\tuint32_t start_time \u003d sys_clock_cycle_get_32();\n#endif\n\t/* This test is trying to test the functionality of crec_usleep, so we\n\t * allow the usage even though it\u0027s in Zephyr code.\n\t */\n\tcrec_usleep(expected_duration); /* NOLINT_EC_SYMBOL */\n#if defined(CONFIG_TIMER_HAS_64BIT_CYCLE_COUNTER)\n\tuint64_t now \u003d sys_clock_cycle_get_64();\n\tuint64_t cycles_elapsed \u003d now - start_time;\n#else\n\tuint32_t now \u003d sys_clock_cycle_get_32();\n\tuint64_t cycles_elapsed \u003d now - start_time;\n#endif\n\tuint64_t sleep_duration \u003d (cycles_elapsed * USEC_PER_SEC) /\n\t\t\t\t  sys_clock_hw_cycles_per_sec();\n```\n[🔗](http://go/tj/aa3b6004-fcef-4922-b971-d711fb06d0d7)",
